WEBVTT

00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:02.085
Previously on Love Live!

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:06.756
In our second year of high school, we catch
wind that our school's getting shut down!

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:09.551
My dazzling high school life...

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:13.513
To prevent it from shutting down, we gotta
increase the number of applying students.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.934
I'm gonna promote my school by becoming
a school idol—they're super popular!

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:18.768
But...

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:20.395
No idols.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:23.648
Focus on how you'll make what
time you have left here count.

00:00:24.482 --> 00:00:27.027
But I still wanna do something for my school!

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:27.986
I can't give up.

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:30.030
I'm definitely gonna do this!

00:00:42.292 --> 00:00:43.501
So early... What is it?

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.504
We thought we'd ask for permission
to use the auditorium!

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:48.632
The student handbook states that...

00:00:48.632 --> 00:00:53.345
students can use the auditorium for
purposes besides club activities.

00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:56.931
The requested date is after school on
the day of the Welcome Party.

00:00:56.931 --> 00:00:58.350
What are you planning?

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.726
Well...

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.685
A concert!

00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:04.439
The three of us chose to
become school idols,

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:07.067
and we're gonna hold our first
concert in the auditorium.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.443
H-Honoka...

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:11.363
W-We don't know if we'll
be able to do that yet...

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:12.989
Huh? Yeah, we will.

00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:13.823
Just a moment.

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:16.284
I never agreed to appear onstage...

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:18.578
Are you really prepared to do this?

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:19.162
Huh?

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:20.580
W-We'll be fine!

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.166
The Welcome Party isn't some game.

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:26.920
Well, they only came to get permission
to use the auditorium, y"know?

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.674
Since they're not even a club, the student
council doesn't have the right...

00:01:30.674 --> 00:01:32.926
to give colorful commentary
about their request.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.135
True, but...

00:01:34.678 --> 00:01:36.346
Excuse us.

00:01:38.014 --> 00:01:39.808
Score!

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:43.144
Why did you take their side?

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.900
No matter how many times I do it,
that's what they guide me to do.

00:01:51.569 --> 00:01:52.779
The cards, I mean.

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:00.078
I'm honoring the divine will of the cards!

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:17.637
<i>Massugu ha omoi ga minna wo musubu Our honest
feelings are what will fie us all together.</i>

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:22.726
Honki demo bukiyou butsukari au kokoro Even with
our clumsy sincerity, our hearts will still collide.

00:02:22.726 --> 00:02:27.480
Sore demo mitaiyo ohkina yume wa And despite
it all, we want to dream a really grand dream.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.068
Koko ni aruyo hajimatta bakari That dream
is here, and it has only now just begun!

00:02:32.068 --> 00:02:33.194
(wakatteru)
(We understand)

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:37.073
Tanoshii dakejanai tamesarerudarou That it's not
all fun and games— we'll face a lot of obstacles.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.074
(wakatteru)
(We understand)

00:02:38.074 --> 00:02:41.828
Datte sono kurushisa mo mirai That those
hardships will be paving our futures...

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:42.912
ikundayo
So here we go!

00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:47.041
Atsumattara tsuyoi jibun ni nattekuyo If we all
join together, we'll be able to become stronger.

00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:51.629
(Kittone) kawari tsuzukete (WE'LL BE A STARY/) (We're sure
that) we will all grow and mature. (We'll become stars!)

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:56.676
Sorezore ga sukina koto de ganbarerunara That's why we feel
that if we give the things that we love the most our all,

00:02:56.676 --> 00:03:01.306
atarashii (basho ga) gohru dane what awaits
then (our new place) will be our goal.

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:06.478
Sorezore no sukina koto wo shinjiteireba That's why we
feel that if we believe in the things we love in our lives,

00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:11.441
tokimeki wo (daite) susumerudarou we can learn to
love (then embrace) our butterflies and advance!

00:03:11.441 --> 00:03:16.988
(kowagaru kuse wa sutechae) tobikiri no egao de So crumple up your
fears, throw them away, and then just put on your brightest smiles!

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:24.537
(tonde tonde takaku) bokura wa ima no naka de (Higher and higher
we"ll fly) The lights that are shining within our hearts...

00:03:25.914 --> 00:03:29.292
kagayaki wo matteta
They're waiting to brighten the world.

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.546
I explained this already.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:37.342
Don't mention any of that idol nonsense,
and simply borrow all that we can.

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:38.259
Why?

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:40.553
Bread again?

00:03:40.845 --> 00:03:44.682
My mom runs a Japanese sweets shop,
so I rarely ever get to eat bread.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:47.936
#2 - Let's be Idols! But before
lunch...? You'll gain weight...

00:03:47.936 --> 00:03:49.771
Maybe.

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:52.690
Hello there.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.275
We saw the bulletin board.

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:56.402
You're going to become school idols?

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.153
What?

00:03:57.153 --> 00:03:59.364
I didn't think you'd do it, Umi-chan.

00:04:00.198 --> 00:04:02.450
Did you put something up
on the bulletin board!?

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.327
Yep! Info about our debut concert.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.038
You never think of others!

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.376
We only have a single month to prepare,
and we have yet to learn anything of note!

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:13.002
You're far too optimistic!

00:04:13.002 --> 00:04:15.505
But Kotori-chan said it'd be fine.

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:19.050
Like...this...

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.552
Kotori?

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:23.638
Yeah, something like this.

00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:26.599
Lookit, I tried to sketch up some
costume designs for our concert.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.687
So cute!

00:04:30.895 --> 00:04:31.855
Really?

00:04:31.855 --> 00:04:36.651
This curvature will be hard to tailor,
but I'll probably figure it out.

00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:37.652
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:04:37.652 --> 00:04:39.070
K-Kotori?

00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:40.738
How about it, Umi-chan?

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.700
Um...

00:04:43.992 --> 00:04:46.411
It's cute, right? Right?

00:04:47.537 --> 00:04:51.624
Th-These long objects here...

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.709
Those are legs.

00:04:53.835 --> 00:04:57.005
Are you saying we're going to wear
tiny skirts and show our bare legs?

00:04:57.005 --> 00:04:58.381
Well, we're idols.

00:05:01.759 --> 00:05:03.595
It's all good!

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.598
Umi-chan, your legs aren't that beefy.

00:05:06.598 --> 00:05:08.641
You're one to talk.

00:05:09.225 --> 00:05:09.767
Huh?

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.651
Fine! I'm going on a diet!

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.029
I think you both look fine...

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.867
We gotta decide on a whole
bunch of things, huh?

00:05:25.867 --> 00:05:28.995
Like autograph signature styles, how to keep
a low profile when we walk around town...

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.080
Both of those ideas are useless.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.498
Before any of that...

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.003
We need to decide on a
name for our idol group.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.218
I'm totally drawing a blank here.

00:05:44.218 --> 00:05:48.014
It'd be easier to think of one if our group
had a unique, charming feature...

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.725
We are all pretty different...

00:05:50.725 --> 00:05:53.895
Then, maybe we'll just use our names?

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:55.939
Honoka-Umi-Kotori!

00:05:55.939 --> 00:05:57.315
Howdy!

00:05:57.315 --> 00:05:58.066
Honoka!

00:05:58.066 --> 00:05:58.733
Umi!

00:05:58.733 --> 00:06:00.068
And Kotori!

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.986
Sounds like a comedy troupe.

00:06:01.986 --> 00:06:02.946
Yeah...

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:04.447
I know!

00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:06.407
Umi-chan, you're Sea!

00:06:06.407 --> 00:06:08.117
Kotori-chan, you're Air!

00:06:08.117 --> 00:06:09.744
And I'm Land!

00:06:09.744 --> 00:06:12.413
Together, we're "Land, Sea, and Air"!

00:06:12.413 --> 00:06:14.499
Protecting the citizens' peace!

00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:16.793
I don't think that sounds idol-y at all...

00:06:16.793 --> 00:06:17.919
Guess not...

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:23.174
Then... Uhhh...

00:06:23.174 --> 00:06:24.217
I know!

00:06:24.425 --> 00:06:26.094
Debut Concert Notice!

00:06:26.094 --> 00:06:27.303
And...Group Name Suggestions!

00:06:27.303 --> 00:06:28.805
That'll do it!

00:06:28.805 --> 00:06:30.306
So you're leaving it to others.

00:06:30.306 --> 00:06:33.184
I bet it'll draw more interest this way.

00:06:33.184 --> 00:06:34.644
Yeah, maybe...

00:06:35.687 --> 00:06:39.023
All right, let's practice our
singing and dancing next!

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:50.368
We'd probably get in people's way here.

00:06:53.538 --> 00:06:55.540
It's jam-packed in here, too.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.500
Um, it's locked.

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:00.086
Is an empty classroom really
out of the question?

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:03.423
An empty classroom, huh?
What do you need one for?

00:07:03.673 --> 00:07:05.883
School idol practice...

00:07:05.883 --> 00:07:08.511
You girls? Idols...?

00:07:10.471 --> 00:07:12.140
Don't laugh!

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.559
So...

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.437
This seems to be the only available space.

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:21.149
There's no shade, and we
can't be out here if it rains...

00:07:21.149 --> 00:07:23.151
But don't look a gift horse
in the mouth, right?

00:07:23.359 --> 00:07:27.697
I guess, but hey—we won't have to
worry about the noise up here.

00:07:27.697 --> 00:07:30.366
All right! We've gotta practice hardcore!

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.828
Let's start with vocal training!

00:07:33.828 --> 00:07:34.579
Right!

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:41.961
Um, what song?

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.130
Don't look at me...

00:07:44.714 --> 00:07:46.132
I dunno!

00:07:54.223 --> 00:07:55.391
Idols...

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.311
Kayo-chin!

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.020
Rin-chan...

00:07:59.353 --> 00:08:00.521
What's up?

00:08:00.521 --> 00:08:03.149
Oh, um...

00:08:03.441 --> 00:08:04.942
N-Nothing...

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:08.029
C'mon, let's head home.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:09.655
Okay.

00:08:16.537 --> 00:08:17.872
What is this?

00:08:17.872 --> 00:08:19.874
Wh-Who knows?

00:08:22.585 --> 00:08:24.003
Oh, welcome.

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.297
Good evening. Is Honoka home?

00:08:26.297 --> 00:08:27.715
She's right upstairs.

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:29.884
How about some dango?

00:08:29.884 --> 00:08:34.097
Homura Manju
No, thank you. I'm trying to watch what I eat.

00:08:34.555 --> 00:08:36.516
Good work today!

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:38.142
How about some dango?

00:08:38.142 --> 00:08:40.228
I'll pour you some tea.

00:08:44.982 --> 00:08:47.693
What about the whole dieting plan?

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.199
You seem to have no
intentions of working hard.

00:08:53.616 --> 00:08:55.827
And? What will our song be?

00:08:56.828 --> 00:08:59.539
I found a first year who's
crazy good at singing.

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:03.960
She's a genius on the piano too, so I bet
she can even compose original stuff.

00:09:04.127 --> 00:09:06.212
I wanna ask her about it tomorrow.

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:11.425
We were saying how if she can compose the
song, we can do something for the lyrics!

00:09:11.425 --> 00:09:13.427
"Something," huh?

00:09:13.427 --> 00:09:15.221
Yep. Right?

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:16.097
Yep!

00:09:19.976 --> 00:09:21.811
Wh-What are you doing?

00:09:22.186 --> 00:09:27.859
Hey Umi-chan, in middle school, didn't you
write some poems and whatnot?

00:09:27.859 --> 00:09:28.359
What?

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:32.530
You let us read them before, didn't you?

00:09:35.324 --> 00:09:36.242
She's escaping!

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:40.705
- Please, that's enough! I'm leaving!
- Come on, come on!

00:09:41.706 --> 00:09:43.291
I refuse!

00:09:43.291 --> 00:09:45.084
What!? C'mon, why?

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:46.127
Aww...

00:09:46.127 --> 00:09:47.295
Absolutely not.

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:51.716
The poems I wrote in middle school are so
childish that I'd prefer to never recall them.

00:09:51.716 --> 00:09:54.468
They say idols gotta throw away their shame.

00:09:54.468 --> 00:09:55.011
No, they don't!

00:09:55.469 --> 00:09:58.764
But I have my hands full making our outfits...

00:09:59.056 --> 00:10:01.267
Then Honoka can do it.

00:10:01.267 --> 00:10:03.644
You're the one who suggested this.

00:10:03.644 --> 00:10:05.605
Yeah, but...

00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:09.609
I no likey manju and dango.

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:11.861
You know she can't do this...

00:10:11.861 --> 00:10:13.029
Well...

00:10:13.029 --> 00:10:15.823
Please. You're the only one
who can, Umi-chan!

00:10:15.823 --> 00:10:20.578
We'll help you brainstorm something
we can mess around with!

00:10:26.918 --> 00:10:28.419
Umi-chan...

00:10:28.794 --> 00:10:29.837
Pretty please!?

00:10:33.549 --> 00:10:37.136
That's a cruel trick, Kotori...

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:38.804
Awesome!

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:40.723
I knew you'd be cool with it!

00:10:40.723 --> 00:10:41.349
However...

00:10:41.349 --> 00:10:42.099
Huh?

00:10:42.683 --> 00:10:45.603
I'll take charge of our practice
schedule till the concert.

00:10:45.603 --> 00:10:47.688
What practice schedule?

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:53.027
Idols seem to be having fun while they sing,
but they keep their bodies moving at all times.

00:10:53.027 --> 00:10:55.529
Despite such exertion, they are able to hold
their smiles and not lose their breath.

00:10:55.529 --> 00:10:57.698
It requires a significant amount of stamina.

00:10:58.032 --> 00:11:01.577
Honoka, could you please demonstrate
some push-ups for us?

00:11:01.577 --> 00:11:02.453
Huh?

00:11:03.287 --> 00:11:04.413
This kind?

00:11:04.413 --> 00:11:06.082
And now give us a smile.

00:11:06.082 --> 00:11:06.666
How's this!?

00:11:07.291 --> 00:11:09.627
Can you keep doing push-ups
with that face?

00:11:14.757 --> 00:11:15.883
Ow!

00:11:15.883 --> 00:11:19.762
Archery Club has helped me
to train myself, but you two...

00:11:19.762 --> 00:11:22.682
You need to gain at least enough stamina
to hold your smiles while singing.

00:11:23.099 --> 00:11:26.227
Oh, my. Being an idol is hard work.

00:11:26.602 --> 00:11:28.354
Right. So...

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:40.199
Five laps is so, so much!

00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:42.535
My legs feel like rubber!

00:11:42.535 --> 00:11:47.081
Starting today, every morning and evening,
in addition to song and dance practice,

00:11:47.081 --> 00:11:49.083
<i>you will engage in physical fitness training.</i>

00:11:49.417 --> 00:11:51.002
Twice a day!?

00:11:51.002 --> 00:11:51.669
Correct.

00:11:51.961 --> 00:11:54.880
If we're going to put on a concert,
we're going to do this right.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.175
Otherwise, we won't be able to
attract any students, right?

00:11:58.175 --> 00:11:59.135
Fine...

00:12:01.762 --> 00:12:04.181
All right! One more, let's go!

00:12:04.181 --> 00:12:05.266
Okay!

00:12:05.266 --> 00:12:06.434
Ladies.

00:12:07.685 --> 00:12:09.437
Vice President?

00:12:10.813 --> 00:12:12.398
That outfit...

00:12:12.398 --> 00:12:14.358
I lend a hand here.

00:12:14.859 --> 00:12:18.863
A shrine is a spiritual place that
gathers all sorts of energies.

00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:25.119
Since you've already climbed the steps,
why not pay a visit to the shrine proper?

00:12:26.704 --> 00:12:29.165
May our first concert go well!

00:12:29.498 --> 00:12:31.834
May it go well!

00:12:31.834 --> 00:12:35.004
They seem pretty serious about this.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.259
Otonokizaka High Idol Club

00:12:49.143 --> 00:12:50.561
Love Live!

00:12:51.729 --> 00:12:53.147
Excuse me!

00:12:56.776 --> 00:12:58.861
Greetings, first years!

00:12:59.362 --> 00:13:02.156
I'm your school idol, Kosaka Honokal!

00:13:04.992 --> 00:13:07.536
Huh? Don't they believe me?

00:13:07.536 --> 00:13:08.621
Of course not!

00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:13.250
So, the girl you mentioned
who's good at singing...

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:13.709
Oh.

00:13:15.211 --> 00:13:17.046
You! Got a minute?

00:13:17.046 --> 00:13:18.172
Me?

00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:19.965
I refuse.

00:13:19.965 --> 00:13:23.344
Please! We want you to be our composer!

00:13:23.344 --> 00:13:24.553
I refuse.

00:13:25.513 --> 00:13:28.557
Maybe you can sing, but can't write...?

00:13:29.517 --> 00:13:31.477
I can write perfectly well.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:35.106
I just don't want to do it, is all.

00:13:35.106 --> 00:13:37.691
We're trying to attract students to our school.

00:13:37.691 --> 00:13:39.402
If we can do that by using your songs...

00:13:39.402 --> 00:13:40.653
Not interested.

00:13:45.241 --> 00:13:48.702
"I refuse"? Sounds like you, Umi.

00:13:48.702 --> 00:13:50.329
It's the most normal response.

00:13:51.914 --> 00:13:55.084
And you went through the trouble
of writing such cool lyrics, too...

00:13:55.084 --> 00:13:56.085
Don't!

00:13:56.085 --> 00:13:59.922
Why not? We're gonna sing it in front of
everyone once we have the music.

00:13:59.922 --> 00:14:01.132
Perhaps, but still...!

00:14:02.341 --> 00:14:03.592
Student Council President?

00:14:04.301 --> 00:14:06.345
Can I borrow you for a moment?

00:14:06.345 --> 00:14:14.979
When "a" and "b" are real numbers, the sum
of "a+b" is known as a complex number.

00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:18.190
The opposite effect, huh?

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:21.694
How will our school look if we try
and fail at using school idols—

00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:25.614
Something we've never had in the past?

00:14:27.283 --> 00:14:29.910
I'd rather not see our school close, either.

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:34.415
But if you truly feel the same way,
I want you to give this more thought.

00:14:35.541 --> 00:14:37.460
Maybe she's right.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:41.422
Maybe this won't be as simple as I thought...

00:14:41.714 --> 00:14:43.841
You finally realized it?

00:14:43.841 --> 00:14:47.011
I didn't suggest it as a joke or anything.

00:14:47.011 --> 00:14:50.181
I'm doing everything your
practice schedule demands.

00:14:50.181 --> 00:14:52.600
But all I've got to show for
it are my sore legs...

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:59.857
I do believe you're trying hard, but consider
the student council president's words.

00:14:59.857 --> 00:15:03.486
You're right. We have less than a month left...

00:15:03.486 --> 00:15:07.323
If we're really putting on a concert,
we'll need to figure out our song.

00:15:07.323 --> 00:15:10.493
We no longer have the time
to find a composer.

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:15.247
We may simply have to sing a cover
of another idol group's song.

00:15:15.998 --> 00:15:17.500
Maybe.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.250
Yeah...

00:15:28.302 --> 00:15:29.887
How's your training coming along?

00:15:30.804 --> 00:15:33.933
If there's anything we can do to
help with the concert, tell us.

00:15:33.933 --> 00:15:35.809
Like the lighting, or ushering...

00:15:35.809 --> 00:15:38.103
There's a lot on your plate, right?

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:39.813
Huh? For real?

00:15:39.813 --> 00:15:40.523
Sure.

00:15:40.981 --> 00:15:44.568
After all, you're doing this for our school.

00:15:44.568 --> 00:15:47.196
Everyone in our class agrees
that we should all help.

00:15:48.656 --> 00:15:50.241
I see...

00:15:50.241 --> 00:15:51.617
You can do it!

00:15:52.409 --> 00:15:53.285
Thanks!

00:15:53.869 --> 00:15:54.954
Bye-bye!

00:15:55.246 --> 00:15:56.497
Bye-bye!

00:16:01.669 --> 00:16:02.545
Someone submitted one!?

00:16:02.545 --> 00:16:03.379
Really!?

00:16:03.379 --> 00:16:05.339
We got one!

00:16:05.339 --> 00:16:06.340
One!

00:16:09.552 --> 00:16:11.262
U's?

00:16:11.595 --> 00:16:13.889
I believe you read that as "Muse."

00:16:13.889 --> 00:16:15.182
Oh, like hair mousse?

00:16:15.182 --> 00:16:16.100
No.

00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:20.104
If memory serves, its etymology stems
from a mythological goddess.

00:16:20.104 --> 00:16:21.522
Uh-huh...

00:16:21.522 --> 00:16:24.441
I think it sounds very sweet. I like it!

00:16:27.027 --> 00:16:28.487
Muse, huh?

00:16:30.948 --> 00:16:34.493
Okay. Starting today, we're "u's"!

00:16:35.119 --> 00:16:37.746
I hear they're always practicing on the roof.

00:16:37.746 --> 00:16:41.750
I didn't know our school had any school idols.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.711
Kayo-chin, ready to go?

00:16:43.711 --> 00:16:44.962
Y-Yeah...

00:16:49.216 --> 00:16:50.426
No one's here.

00:16:50.426 --> 00:16:51.218
Meow?

00:16:51.218 --> 00:16:53.012
Hey, where's that one girl?

00:16:53.012 --> 00:16:53.721
That one girl?

00:16:53.971 --> 00:16:57.600
Do you mean Nishikino-san?
The girl who's really good at singing?

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.603
Yeah, her! So she goes
by Nishikino-san, huh?

00:17:00.603 --> 00:17:03.480
Yes. Nishikino Maki-san.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:08.068
I wanted to have a chat with her,
but I guess she went home already.

00:17:08.819 --> 00:17:10.904
She might be in the music room.

00:17:10.904 --> 00:17:12.031
Why there?

00:17:12.031 --> 00:17:15.242
She isn't very social...

00:17:15.242 --> 00:17:19.872
She's always in the library during breaks,
and the music room after school.

00:17:20.497 --> 00:17:21.999
Gotcha.

00:17:23.208 --> 00:17:25.252
Thanks, you two.

00:17:25.252 --> 00:17:25.919
Excuse me!

00:17:29.632 --> 00:17:33.260
P-Please do your best at...being idols.

00:17:37.097 --> 00:17:38.766
Yeah, naturally!

00:17:44.104 --> 00:17:45.356
What do you want now?

00:17:45.648 --> 00:17:48.525
I thought I'd ask again...

00:17:48.525 --> 00:17:49.943
You're persistent.

00:17:49.943 --> 00:17:54.198
Yeah, I guess. Umi-chan always
gets mad at me for that.

00:17:54.198 --> 00:17:57.159
I don't even listen to that type of music.

00:17:57.576 --> 00:18:00.287
I prefer classical and jazz.

00:18:00.287 --> 00:18:02.206
Really? Why is that?

00:18:02.206 --> 00:18:05.376
Because pop music is so
light and lacks substance.

00:18:05.834 --> 00:18:07.211
Like they're playing around.

00:18:07.503 --> 00:18:08.712
True enough.

00:18:09.046 --> 00:18:09.588
Huh?

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:11.924
I actually felt the same way.

00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:18.430
I thought we were going to party
it up and have fun singing...

00:18:18.806 --> 00:18:21.517
But it's actually pretty hard work.

00:18:23.977 --> 00:18:26.355
I know! Can you do push-ups?

00:18:26.355 --> 00:18:27.231
What?

00:18:27.231 --> 00:18:28.649
Oh, you can't? Too bad.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.944
O-Of course I can!

00:18:32.236 --> 00:18:35.447
One, two, three.

00:18:35.739 --> 00:18:37.491
Are you satisfied now?

00:18:37.491 --> 00:18:40.160
Pretty impressive!
Doing better than I did!

00:18:40.828 --> 00:18:43.580
Of course I am. Actually, I'm—

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.249
Okay, now do some while smiling.

00:18:45.999 --> 00:18:46.750
Why?

00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:47.960
C'mon.

00:18:56.635 --> 00:18:59.012
See? Being an idol's pretty hard, right?

00:18:59.346 --> 00:19:00.514
What are you talking about?

00:19:02.224 --> 00:19:03.559
Jeez...

00:19:03.559 --> 00:19:04.977
Here, our lyrics.

00:19:04.977 --> 00:19:06.645
Try reading them once.

00:19:06.979 --> 00:19:08.355
I told you, I...

00:19:08.355 --> 00:19:10.107
Reading them can't hurt, right?

00:19:10.107 --> 00:19:11.400
I'll ask you about them later.

00:19:11.984 --> 00:19:15.404
If you still don't wanna do it,
I'll leave you alone.

00:19:18.115 --> 00:19:20.409
My answer isn't going to change.

00:19:20.826 --> 00:19:22.536
It's okay if it doesn't.

00:19:22.536 --> 00:19:24.955
If that's the case, let me
listen to you sing again.

00:19:25.748 --> 00:19:28.792
I love your voice, Nishikino-san.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:35.299
I'm asking you to compose for us because
your song and piano playing moved me!

00:19:38.844 --> 00:19:44.475
We train at the local shrine every morning
and evening, so drop by if you'd like.

00:19:45.267 --> 00:19:48.937
I love your voice, Nishikino-san.

00:19:51.523 --> 00:19:53.525
No more, no more!

00:19:56.028 --> 00:19:57.154
I feel like jelly.

00:19:57.154 --> 00:20:01.950
Not good enough. You still have two
laps left. Or are you giving up!?

00:20:03.035 --> 00:20:04.995
Umi-chan, you're a slave driver!

00:20:04.995 --> 00:20:08.624
I think it's more accurate to call
her a wicked drill sergeant...

00:20:12.044 --> 00:20:13.212
What was that?

00:20:13.212 --> 00:20:14.505
I dunno.

00:20:14.505 --> 00:20:16.298
Wh-Wh—

00:20:16.298 --> 00:20:18.008
What are you doing!?

00:20:18.008 --> 00:20:20.636
You've still got some growing to do.

00:20:20.803 --> 00:20:21.804
What!?

00:20:21.804 --> 00:20:24.223
But you haven't given up on your
desires yet, so there's still hope.

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:26.517
You might continue to blossom.

00:20:26.517 --> 00:20:27.643
What're you talking about?

00:20:28.352 --> 00:20:31.855
If you're too embarrassed about
something, there's always anonymity.

00:20:33.148 --> 00:20:34.191
What are you...?

00:20:34.191 --> 00:20:35.359
You know what I mean.

00:20:44.076 --> 00:20:45.410
See you later!

00:20:46.078 --> 00:20:48.330
Hey, sis!

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:51.583
Is this thing for you?
It isn't labeled...

00:20:51.959 --> 00:20:54.419
Well, except it says "u's" on it.

00:20:54.419 --> 00:20:55.087
What?

00:21:00.843 --> 00:21:01.885
This is...!

00:21:05.514 --> 00:21:06.473
Here we go.

00:21:14.106 --> 00:21:18.235
I SAY...
This voice...

00:21:18.235 --> 00:21:21.029
HEY! HEY! HEY, START DASH!

00:21:21.697 --> 00:21:24.616
Amazing... It's a real song...

00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:28.203
HEY! HEY! HEY, START DASH!
It's our...

00:21:29.454 --> 00:21:31.123
Our own song...

00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:37.296
Even baby birds swaddled in down will
someday flap their wings and take to the sky.

00:21:37.296 --> 00:21:42.634
They'll soar up high with wings that grow big
and strong. Look, we're getting some votes!

00:21:43.635 --> 00:21:49.766
Don't you ever think of giving up—
such a grand day is sure to come.

00:21:49.766 --> 00:21:56.523
You will feel the soft beating of wings that signal this new beginning.
- C'mon, let's practice! - Yeah!

00:22:14.917 --> 00:22:20.547
Sunao ni oikakete yuukide oikakete Chase after
it with honesty, chase after it with courage.

00:22:20.797 --> 00:22:26.094
Chiisana negai ga ashita wo tsukuru That one
small wish is what will help to create tomorrow.

00:22:26.386 --> 00:22:32.517
Dekirukamo minna ga nozomunara It might
be possible if we all want it to come true.

00:22:32.517 --> 00:22:39.441
Dare yori ganbacchae tonikaku Jjounetsu no mama ni Give it
more effort than anyone else and stay as passionate as ever.

00:22:39.441 --> 00:22:44.488
Mezasu no wa kireina kaze fuku michi Let's aim to
find our path while riding on a beautiful wind.

00:22:45.405 --> 00:22:50.953
Hane no youni ude agete Spread your
arms out wide like they're your own wings.

00:22:50.953 --> 00:22:56.208
Mabushii mirai e to tobuyo We'll use
them to take off into our bright future.

00:22:57.417 --> 00:23:03.715
Kitto seishun ga kikoeru sono shunkan ni kikoeru You can hear the
songs filled with our youth, you can hear it in this one moment.

00:23:04.174 --> 00:23:09.388
Egao nara itsu no hi mo daijoubu As long as
we see you smiling, every day is worth it!

00:23:09.388 --> 00:23:15.769
Kitto seishun ga kikoeru sono shunkan ga mitaine You can hear the
songs filled with our youth, we want to see you at that moment.

00:23:15.769 --> 00:23:21.650
Tonari ni kimi ga ite (ureshii keshiki) I want you
to be right beside me. (It's such happy scenery.)

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:27.072
Tonari wa kimi nanda
Only when the one right there is you.

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:39.292
Next time on Love Live!
"First Concert!"
